  era: "Section 1 \xB7 Prehistoric India \xB7 c. 1.5 million years ago \u2013 700 BCE"
  title: Middle Palaeolithic
  text: 'From roughly 385,000 years ago, toolmakers turned to smaller flake tools: scrapers, borers and points struck from carefully prepared cores. Middle Palaeolithic sites are found across India, including the Belan valley, Bhimbetka, and Nevasa on the Pravara river.'
